{
  "id": "29661_yobitomeru",
  "headword": "{呼|よ}び{止|と}める",
  "reading": "よびとめる",
  "romaji": "yobitomeru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb",
  "gloss": "to call out and stop; to hail",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to call out and stop; to hail",
      "explanation": "To make someone who is passing or leaving stop by calling out to them."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29661_yobitomeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{通行人|つうこうにん}を{呼|よ}び{止|と}める。",
      "english": "To call out and stop a passerby.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29661_yobitomeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{警官|けいかん}に{呼|よ}び{止|と}められた。",
      "english": "I was stopped by a police officer.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29661_yobitomeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{帰|かえ}ろうとしたところを{同僚|どうりょう}に{呼|よ}び{止|と}められた。",
      "english": "Just as I was about to leave, a colleague called out and stopped me.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Transitive ichidan verb. Xを{呼|よ}び{止|と}める. A compound of {呼|よ}ぶ (to call) and {止|と}める (to stop): the calling out is what makes the person stop. Frequently used in the passive, {呼|よ}び{止|と}められる, when one is stopped by police or a stranger.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {警官|けいかん}に{呼|よ}び{止|と}められる: to be stopped by a police officer\n- {大声|おおごえ}で{呼|よ}び{止|と}める: to call out loudly to stop someone\n- {店員|てんいん}を{呼|よ}び{止|と}める: to flag down a shop clerk",
